{title: A Thousand Tongues}
{key: E}

{comment: Verse 1}
O [E]for a thousand tongues to sing my great Redeemer's [B]praise,
The [E]glories of my [A]God and King, the [E]triumphs of [B]His [E]grace!

{comment: Verse 2}
My [E]gracious Master and my God,assist me to [B]proclaim,
To [E]spread through all the [A]earth abroad the [E]honors of [B]Thy [E]name.

{comment: Chorus}
All [A]glory to [E/G#]You, All [B]glory to You[E]
[A]Forever, and [E/G#]ever, and [B]ever
All [A]glory to [E/G#]You, All [B]glory to You[E]
[A]Forever, and [E/G#]ever, and [B]ever Amen    [E]

{comment: Verse 3}
[E]Jesus! the name that charms our fears, that bids our sorrows [B]cease;
'Tis [E]music in the [A]sinner's ears, 'tis [E]life, and health, and [B]pe[E]ace.

{comment: Verse 4}
He [E]breaks the power of canceled sin, He sets the prisoner [B]free;
His [E]blood can [A]make the foulest clean; His [E]blood availed [B]for [E]me.
